-- title:
--   Specialisation of the H₁ chart yields a κ(A)-algebra homomorphism
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ its residue field is written $\kappa(A)$, and for an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the notation $\mathcal{O}$ abbreviates `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ of $k_0$, with residue field $\kappa(\mathcal{O})$.
--
--   The data are: a prime $q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa(A)$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the places satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q M' (ResidueField A)`; a distinguished element $s$ of $W$; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) in `fieldBar q M'`, that is in the corresponding base change of `xHFunctionFieldC ℚ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; and a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of that subring, a map on places, and the compatibilities with $A$ and with orders recorded in the structure `ConstantReduction`. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read back as a Laurent series over $\kappa(A)$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Local data at $q$ (the group `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ`): an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $\mathcal{O}$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, $\mathcal{O}$ is Henselian local, $\kappa(\mathcal{O})$ is algebraically closed, and every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Level and cyclotomic data: an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity, together with `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$; a subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` is the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$; an intermediate field $K$ of $k_0 \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` which by `hK` equals `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, regarded as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$; and an element $j \in K$ which as a Laurent series is `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq`, the coefficientwise image over $k_0$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, with $j \neq 0$.
--
--   Functoriality hypotheses for Weierstrass level structures, stated for all commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $T$: `hℓ` says that `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` (the affine equation at $(x_P,y_P)$, vanishing of $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi\,\ell_g)$ at $x_P$, and $x_Q = x_P$, $y_Q = y_P$) is preserved on passing to $C \bullet W$ and `D.variableChange C`, for every variable change $C$; `hM` says that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (which is `W.IsTwoKernel h` when $p^k = 2$ and `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise) is preserved on passing to $C \bullet W$ and `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; `hL` says that if $h$ divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` then `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` divides `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u^{-2}(x - r))` for the coefficients $u, r$ of $C$. Further, a system of group laws $\mathcal{G}$ on $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with `h𝒢` (chord–tangent: for each projective Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant the relative group law admits a points-evaluation) and `h𝒢O` (the origin is the identity: a ring homomorphism from the origin chart ring realising the identity section and killing the coordinates $x/y$ and $z/y$); a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for $\mathcal{G}$ and $q$, with `h𝒯` requiring its section transport property in its two clauses, for variable changes and for coefficient homomorphisms; `hVC`, the existence, for every projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and every variable change $C$, of a graded ring homomorphism from `projModelGradingCR W` to `projModelGradingCR (C • W)` pushing the irrelevant ideal above the irrelevant ideal of the target and satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom W C`; and `hCO`, the analogous existence of graded ring homomorphisms satisfying `IsCoefficientHom W f.toRingHom` for every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $f : T \to T'$.
--
--   Write $\mathcal{R}$ for [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.rigidDataH1Pow ↥𝒪 ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L65) and $D = \mathcal{R}$`.toLevelModuliDatum`. The moduli data are: an abstract representing package $P_0$ for $D$ over $\mathcal{O}$, consisting of a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $P_0.B_0$ with a universal point such that every point of $D$ over an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$ is the image of the universal point under a unique $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $P_0.B_0 \to T$; a point $x_0$ of $D$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant `D.jOf x₀`, read as a Laurent series over $k_0$, is `jqNModC ↥k₀ q`, i.e. `qExpand ↥k₀ q (jqModC ↥k₀)`; an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism `clC` from $P_0.B_0$ to the chart algebra [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥𝒪 ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over `Algebra.adjoin ↥𝒪 {j}`, which by `hclC` lifts the classifying homomorphism `P₀.classify x₀` of $x_0$ value by value. Finally, a ring homomorphism $\theta : \kappa(\mathcal{O}) \to \kappa(A)$ compatible with the two residue maps along the inclusion $\mathcal{O} \subseteq A$ (hypothesis `hθ`), and a $\kappa(A)$-subalgebra $S$ of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` characterised by `hS`: an element $f$ lies in $S$ precisely when $f$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $w$ of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa(A)$ which is rational (the structure map $\kappa(A) \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ being surjective) and whose valuation subring contains `jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`.
--
--   The conclusion is the following. For every maximal ideal $y$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin ↥𝒪 ↥K j` and every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\psi$ from that chart algebra to $\kappa(\mathcal{O})$ whose zero set is exactly $y$ (for all $c$ in the chart algebra, $\psi(c) = 0$ if and only if $c \in y$), there exists a $\kappa(A)$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : S \to \kappa(A)$ with the following property, valid for all admissible functions simultaneously. Let $gf$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, assume that its coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` (hypothesis `hgi`), and assume cusp regularity: for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order, the image of $gf$ also has non-negative order at $P$. Assume moreover that `coeffEmb ↥k₀ gf` lies in $K$ and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in the chart algebra `chartAlgFin ↥𝒪 ↥K j`. Then the $R_0$-residue of $gf$, an element of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, belongs to $S$, and its value under $\chi$ equals $\theta$ applied to $\psi$ evaluated at the element of the chart algebra determined by `coeffEmb ↥k₀ gf`.
--
--   This is the $H_1$-level form of the statement that the readings of a $\kappa(\mathcal{O})$-point of the integral chart of the modular curve on admissible modular functions are realised, uniformly in the function, by a single $\kappa(A)$-algebra homomorphism on the subalgebra $S$ of functions regular at the rational places where the geometric $j$-invariant is regular. It is the algebraic input for [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_forall_evalAt_eq_apply_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_forall_evalAt_eq_apply_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow), which converts such a homomorphism into a place of the special fibre, in the study of the reduction of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-structure at the prime $q$.
